# Cooking (audio processing) tuning — passed through to cook.sh.
# COOK_PARALLEL: how many tracks to encode concurrently for zip downloads
#   (flac, oggflac, vorbis, aac, opus, mp3, wav*). Defaults to nproc (number of
#   CPUs); more than that gives no speedup and only wastes RAM. Leave unset to
#   auto-detect, or pin it (e.g. 2 on a 2-CPU server).
# COOK_CPUS: CPU affinity range for taskset (e.g. "0-7"). Empty = no pinning (default).
# COOK_SCHED_IDLE: set to 1 ONLY on a dedicated box to run cooking at idle CPU/IO
#   priority. On a shared/small server leave it unset — idle priority starves the
#   encoders and makes downloads take absurdly long.
# COOK_PARALLEL=2
# COOK_CPUS=
# COOK_SCHED_IDLE=
